{"symbol":"is_ip_address","type":"function","file":"aiohttp/helpers.py","lines":[491,501],"source":"def is_ip_address(host: str | None) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if host looks like an IP Address.\n\n    This check is only meant as a heuristic to ensure that\n    a host is not a domain name.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not host:\n        return False\n    # For a host to be an ipv4 address, it must be all numeric.\n    # The host must contain a colon to be an IPv6 address.\n    return \":\" in host or host.replace(\".\", \"\").isdigit()","calls":[],"called_by":[],"confidence":0.92,"purpose":"Check if host looks like an IP Address."}
